 "final": {
  "slips": [
   "Here is what stands behind my yes. I'm your Venus in Taurus in the tenth house, and I sit directly opposite your Pluto in Scorpio in the fourth. So what you love out in the open is always facing what you guard at the root.",
   "Your Pluto is at home in Scorpio and retrograde, and it rules your fifth house, where courtship and delight live. That's why an attraction in you doesn't stay light for long. It drops into that private, rooted place where you keep what you can't afford to lose, and then you guard it like a secret when you could offer it like a gift.",
   "Because of that opposition, I want to hold him the way I'd hold a rose, tightly by the stem. Your Pluto treats keeping the secret as a kind of power. Between the two of us, silence starts to feel like safety, when really we are both gripping the same thing from opposite ends.",
   "That opposition is also the spine of a kite in your chart. Its wings are your Moon in Pisces and your Jupiter exalted in Cancer, both trine your Pluto and both sextile me. So the pressure has somewhere to go: into feeling said honestly, and into a generosity that doesn't keep score.",
   "In practice, let the Moon and Jupiter carry it. Tell him what you feel, not what you need him to do about it, and don't ask for an answer that same evening. That way your Pluto keeps its dignity, and I get to be generous instead of possessive.",
   "So tell me honestly: if he answered kindly but didn't feel the same, would you let the feeling change shape, or would you hold on to it harder?"
